{
  "$id": "https://archlens.dev/schemas/revision_diff-1.1.schema.json",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "Structured diff between two source states of one logical subject, emitted by 'archlens diff'. This is a DERIVED, explicitly non-authoritative output: it carries an independent format version and must never be read back as measurement evidence. The authoritative measurement remains the two Artifact 1.7 runs it references.\n\nFour concepts are kept separate throughout and must not be conflated by a consumer: logical subject identity ('subject'), source/revision identity ('source_identity_changes'), analyzed-scope identity ('analysis_scope_hash'), and measurement-contract compatibility ('comparability'). A changed 'analysis_scope_hash' means different bytes were analyzed; it is never by itself a statement that the two sides are incomparable.\n\n'metric_attribution' is reconciliation from recorded per-file contributions, not causal inference. A non-zero 'residual' is a finding, not something to explain away. Rename evidence is typed and never inferred from similarity: only a one-to-one exact content match is called a rename.",
